WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.820
My name is Laila White.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.060
It's my artistic name.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:12.960
I'm a dancer.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.200
Photographer and visual artist.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:24.240
I'm a brunette, with curly hair
and a ponytail.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.500
I'm wearing a floral print blouse,

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:36.540
blue jeans and behind me
there are some orange crutches.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:42.460
I'm sitting in front of the painting
of Theodoros Stamos

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.313
and throughout this interview

00:00:44.313 --> 00:00:47.920
some images of me
are going to be shown.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.860
I started dancing in the dark
when I was young.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.060
I didn't know I was going to be
a dancer or a photographer.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:05.240
I was bullied a lot in high school
and when I got home,

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:08.890
I would lock myself in my room,
I would turn off the lights

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.000
and put on some music.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.560
And...

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.113
I wanted to feel the sensation
that my body felt to express

00:01:18.113 --> 00:01:20.110
the pain, the rage...

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:23.260
And then I link it a little bit
with photography.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:27.218
But I never, at any time,
put it in my mind

00:01:27.218 --> 00:01:29.760
that I wanted to be a dancer,
because I thought...

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:33.435
"with a disability I can't be a dancer"

00:01:33.435 --> 00:01:36.490
because at that time
I didn't know anybody.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:43.260
Years later a person gave me
the opportunity to be able to move.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:50.578
That's when I started training myself,
dancing with collectives

00:01:50.578 --> 00:01:52.290
and going to workshops.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.900
I also started to mix it with
photography,

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:59.003
because for me photography
has something very special

00:01:59.003 --> 00:02:01.503
that I don't usually show to everybody.

00:02:01.503 --> 00:02:06.280
I started with photography,
because I have a twin sister,

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.000
from whom I've been separated
since I was very young...

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:15.140
I was trying to find the other face
that I couldn't see for all these years.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:19.400
The photography is a reflection 
of my twin sister.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.100
I'm interested in the general movement,

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:34.170
in the movement of the body,
in the expression of the body.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.890
I started to study a little bit

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.790
how people walked and if these legs
could also say something

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:49.060
about the way they walked,
the position that the feet took.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:52.420
So that's when I got curious.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.780
If I could take that movement 
to the stage, what would happen?

00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:03.243
Each body has a way of explaining 
and expressing itself,

00:03:03.243 --> 00:03:06.058
without using words,
simply through movement

00:03:06.058 --> 00:03:09.928
we are able to express a lot of things.

00:03:09.928 --> 00:03:17.000
My interest is in this movement
and in the image in a scene.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:23.273
During the COVID pandemic,
I started to create a piece

00:03:23.273 --> 00:03:30.635
and that's when I started to create
about some ideas that I have,

00:03:30.635 --> 00:03:36.325
which is about a dream that I had
and that I still have often,

00:03:36.325 --> 00:03:39.800
which is...

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.980
going out without crutches.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:46.603
So the idea has been around
for a long time.

00:03:46.603 --> 00:03:52.633
And I had the opportunity
to bring it into a space

00:03:52.633 --> 00:04:00.610
and how I can translate the dream
into a performance space.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:04.288
And I started to work
on the weight of the dream,

00:04:04.288 --> 00:04:08.380
because it felt so agonising,
so much anguish...

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:11.980
because I felt very anguished
for not having my crutches.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:15.678
And over the years I understood
that maybe this dream

00:04:15.678 --> 00:04:17.460
that my twin sister...

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:24.300
is giving me the opportunity to feel
a sensation that I could never feel.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.362
I feel very fortunate...

00:04:33.362 --> 00:04:36.603
to have chosen what is 
meant for me.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.233
But then I also think
what about my twin sister?

00:04:40.233 --> 00:04:43.828
If she had the chance
to live through this...

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.518
would I...

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.843
Exchange for a moment 
our experience...

00:04:50.843 --> 00:04:56.450
that each one of us could have
the opportunity to live for ourselves.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.568
It's hard to explain.

00:05:01.568 --> 00:05:05.650
There are things that can't be explained
and have no reason why.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.923
When you realise that you've had

00:05:09.923 --> 00:05:14.088
two very different and complicated lives
at the same time,

00:05:14.088 --> 00:05:18.122
you can't question what's easy
or what you can choose.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:22.678
If I was chosen at the time,
when I came to Spain,

00:05:24.153 --> 00:05:25.890
it was for a reason.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:29.352
I always think that I was chosen
for something.

00:05:30.558 --> 00:05:39.020
I don't know what I'm going to do,
but I'm here to do something.

